**Memo**

To: Sarah Thompson, Director of Operations  
From: Michael Chen, Senior Geologist  
Date: October 10, 2023  
Subject: Update on Exploration and Development Activities in the North Dakota Region  

As we continue to expand our efforts in the Bakken Formation, I wanted to provide an update on our drilling and refining initiatives, as well as our pipeline development. On October 5, 2023, our drilling team successfully completed the first phase of the Tundra-5 well located in Williams County, which has demonstrated promising initial flow rates of approximately 1,200 barrels of oil per day. This well is part of our strategic plan to boost production by 15% by the end of Q2 2024.

In collaboration with Apex Refinery, we are also working on enhancing our processing capabilities. The refinery, which is currently undergoing a $10 million upgrade, is expected to increase its throughput capacity by 20% once the modifications are complete by January 2024. This upgrade is crucial for accommodating the anticipated higher production volumes from our drilling activities.

Additionally, I want to highlight our partnership with TransNorth Pipelines, which is set to begin construction on a new pipeline segment connecting our Tundra operations to the main trunk line. This project is scheduled to break ground on November 1, 2023, and is projected to be completed by early Q3 2024. The new pipeline will facilitate the efficient transport of crude oil, reducing logistical costs by an estimated 12% and ensuring that we can meet the demand from Apex Refinery on a timely basis.

Overall, our exploration efforts have revealed significant reserves in the area, with estimates suggesting that we could tap into an additional 2 million barrels over the next year. As we move forward, close coordination with our partners at Apex and TransNorth will be essential to ensure that our production targets are met and that we optimize our operations across the board. 

Please let me know if you require further details or specific data related to any of these projects.

Best,  
